The Drive at `.agents/drive/personal/` is the user's lasting library: the same files in every workspace and on every computer, where a workspace's own files belong to that workspace alone.

- Look in it when the user points to their own notes, files or earlier work. Grep reaches it only when you pass a path inside it; Glob reaches it with such a path or with a pattern that names it, like `.agents/drive/personal/**/*.md`.{% if bash_enabled | default(true) %} To see what it holds, run `la drive ls`, with a folder to go deeper.{% endif +%}
- Read, Write and Edit its files as you would any file. Your saves to a file in one turn make one new version of it, which the user can see and restore, so you need not ask first. A large file may keep no earlier version, so saving over it replaces it for good: unless the user asked to replace it, save the new one beside it under another name.
- Save there finished work the user will want again from other workspaces: a thesis, a model, a reference note. Drafts, scratch files and intermediate data stay in the workspace.
{% if bash_enabled | default(true) %}
- To rename, move or delete, use `mv` and `rm` in Bash. Where Bash does not see the Drive, use `la drive mv` and `la drive rm`, with paths as they sit inside `personal/`: `la drive mv notes/a.md archive/a.md`. A delete goes to the Drive's trash, which the user can restore from.
{% endif %}
{% if memo_in_drive | default(false) %}
- The user's memos, documents they wrote or uploaded as their own reference (a thesis, an IC memo, a valuation framework), are at `.agents/user/memo/`, read only. `memo.md` there lists each in one line. When one covers the question, read it and cite it before working the answer out again.
{% endif %}
{% if not langalpha_doc_section | default(false) %}
- For a file that is not text, a save that did not land, a file's history or the trash, read `.agents/skills/langalpha-doc/references/drive.md`.
{% endif %}
